Generated operation description:
1. Sort the data by departure time (ascending order) and then by arrival time (ascending order within each departure time). This will help in identifying any flights with unrealistic durations more easily.

2. Iterate through the sorted data, comparing the departure time of a flight with the arrival time of the next flight for the same airline. If the arrival time is before the departure time, mark that flight as having an unrealistic duration.

3. After iterating through all flights, filter out the flights with unrealistic durations from the original dataset.

Here's a Python example using pandas library:

```python
import pandas as pd

# Assuming df is your DataFrame and it contains the data you provided
df = pd.DataFrame({...}) # replace the ... with your actual data

# Sort the data by departure time (ascending order) and then by arrival time (ascending order within each departure time)
df = df.sort_values(by=['Departure Time', 'Arrival Time'])

unrealistic_durations = []
for i in range(len(df)):
    if i < len(df)-1 and df.iloc[i]['Airline'] == df.iloc[i+1]['Airline']:
        if df.iloc[i+1]['Arrival Time'] < df.iloc[i]['Departure Time']:
            unrealistic_durations.append(df.iloc[i]['Flight'])

# Filter out the flights with unrealistic durations from the original dataset
df = df[~df['Flight'].isin(unrealistic_durations)]
```

This script will give you a DataFrame containing only the flights without unrealistic durations.
